  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PTEC Unit Conditioner - Application 6646 (Fan Coil Unit Two-Stage Cooling and Electric Heat)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6646-fan-coil-2-stage-cooling-electric-heat",
  "short_model": "PTEC Fan Coil 2-Stage Cooling 6646",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6646",
    "Application 6646",
    "App 6646",
    "550-496PA",
    "Siemens fan coil electric heat",
    "Unit Conditioner"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Fan coil unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Fan coil units with up to two cooling stages (2-position valves or compressors) and up to three electric heat stages, on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller 550-496PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6646 runs a fan coil unit with staged cooling and electric heat on a Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller over BACnet MS/TP. The cooling loop switches up to two stages (2-position valves or compressors) at set loop percentages with minimum on and off times, and the heating loop time-modulates up to three electric heat stages. The fan runs in day mode or cycles with demand.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "CLG STG CNT (AO 75) and HTG STG CNT (AO 88) set how many cooling and heating stages are used.",
    "Both cooling stages are off in heating mode."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Conditioner - Fan Coil Unit Two-Stage Cooling and Electric Heat, Application 6646, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1173",
    "revision_date": "2014-07-17",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/L7SSrBCn3y4Q~8CKKeP~EA/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the unit to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, and reads room temperature, fan, cooling and heating stage status and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 46",
        "name": "FAN",
        "why": "Fan on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 41",
        "name": "CLG STG 1",
        "why": "Cooling stage 1 on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 43",
        "name": "HTG STG 1",
        "why": "Electric heat stage 1 on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6691."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The controller keeps all associated equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, staging times and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
      "Cooling stages honour CLG MIN ON and CLG MIN OFF before they switch, so a stage may lag the loop output."
    ]
  },
